# R7 regression test: an incomplete primary axis set must fail fast
# instead of silently re-indexing the declared extra axis.
#
# Legacy evidence: on `develop` the toolhead built its axis map from the
# axes found in the config, so an "XYA" configuration (X and Y but no Z)
# associated the *extra* axis A with the index of the unconfigured Z axis
# (fixed there by f557a14b).  With the current `extra_axes` design the
# primary axes always occupy indices 0-2 and extra axes start at index 4,
# so the mis-association is structurally impossible AND the incomplete
# primary set is rejected outright with an error naming the missing
# section.  This fixture pins that fail-fast behaviour: no configuration
# may be accepted with fewer than three primary axes, because such a
# configuration would leave an axis slot unowned.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG extra_axis_partial_axes.cfg
SHOULD_FAIL
